     Claudio C Zoppi, Rodrigo Hohl, Fernando C Silva, Fernanda L Lazarim, Joaquim MF Antunes Neto, Mirtes...
     PMC2129167 · Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition · 2006-01-01
     https://doi.org/10.1186/1550-2783-3-2-37
     "This study investigated vitamin C and E supplementation in professional soccer players during training. Supplementation reduced lipid peroxidation and muscle damage but did not improve performance."

  8. The effects of antioxidant vitamin supplementation on resistance exercise induced lipid peroxidation in trained and untrained participants
     Peter E Viitala, Ian J Newhouse, Norm LaVoie, Christine Gottardo
     PMC479696 · Lipids in Health and Disease · 2004-01-01
     https://doi.org/10.1186/1476-511X-3-14
     "This study investigated the impact of vitamin E supplementation on exercise-induced lipid peroxidation in trained and untrained individuals. Vitamin E supplementation did not reduce oxidative damage, and training status did not affect lipid peroxidation levels post-exercise."

